4-602.13 The following non-food contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
1) walk-in cooler shelves (food splash/general buildup/mold);
2) shelf and baking sheet holding panko breading (food debris/general buildup);
3) inside reach-in cooler on cook line used for flour storage (general buildup);
4) fryers - sides and bottom compartments (grease/food debris); and
5) side of kitchen ice machine (dust).
Ensure cleaning of non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed.
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.
